From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:43:27 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 56/76] flashnext cuda: --pp 2, the two ranks as pipeline
 stages over the rank link

Rank 0 holds layers [0, split), the embedding, the n-gram block and the head;
rank 1 holds [split, 48). The boundary rows cross by NCCL send and receive on
the compute stream; rank 1 replays each leader op on its own layers, and the
hello proves both ranks' split (TF_FLASHNEXT_PP_SPLIT, default 24).

Placement memory counts a stage's own layers, in the stored formats too (block
FP8 experts load whole at world 1); the draft head stays on rank 0. Stages keep
no prompt states yet: the cache defaults to 0, and a prompt cache, --spill-gib
or --learn-conversations is refused by name. The serve flag --pp takes 1 to 64;
above 1 it is refused for every other family and backend, above 2 for Flash
Next, and with --tp above 1. TF_FLASHNEXT_PEER_SLOTS' mapped buffer opens for
tensor ranks only.
